# Plan D — Sub-project B: Framework AgentX Subagent (+ dlmod convergence) — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Make `app_moxa_framework` an AgentX subagent that answers its owned config OIDs in-process (no snmpd→nginx→actix HTTP hop), and converge the ~20 dlmod plugins onto it.

**Architecture:** Four new libs — `lib_moxa_snmp_agentx` (C, FRR-style net-snmp subagent wrapper) + `lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx` (Rust FFI); `lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs` (C, OID↔URI mapping seed) + `lib_moxa_rust_ies_auto_mibs` (Rust FFI). A subagent thread in `app_moxa_framework` registers owned OIDs; each handler maps OID→URI then calls `rust_moxa_config_layer::config_operation::{get_config_from_path,update_config}` in-process. Ownership via remove-dlmod-`.conf` + extend `agentx_owned.list` (Plan C mechanism). ISS stays a separate subagent, unchanged.

**Tech Stack:** net-snmp 5.9.3 (AgentX subagent API), C, Rust (actix-web / tokio), buildroot, RFC 2741 AgentX.

